and upper esophageal dysmotility</article-title><source>Dig Dis Sci</source><year>1981</year><volume>26</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>376</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7238266</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Difficulty in swallowing as an early sign</article-title><source>Clin Pediatric</source><year>1971</year><volume>10</volume><issue>11</issue><fpage>682</fpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Endocrine diseases and anaethesia. A review of anae management in pitutary, adrenal and thyroid diseases</article-title><source>Anaethesia</source><year>1970</year><volume>25</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>232</fpage><lpage>52</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holmes</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hooper</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>B.W.R: Anaethesia for thyroid surgery</article-title><source>Anaeth Intensive care</source><year>1973</year><volume>1</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>218</fpage><lpage>25</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lucente</surname><given-names>FE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Endocrine problems in otolaryngology</article-title><source>Ann Otol Rhinol Laryngol</source><year>1973</year><volume>82</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-t